Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Wire=20the=20Transa=C3=A7=C3=B5es=20screen's=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?contributions=20into=20goals,=20reserve=20and=20retirement?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rename the Gastos screen to Transações and make entrada/saída/investimento
visually distinct (icon + color + sign per type), instead of a single
"income vs everything else" split. More importantly, fix the actual gap
behind that request: a transaction created here previously had no way to
touch a goal's progress at all (no goalId field existed on this form), so
"aportar" only worked from the Sonhos screen's own button. Any contribution
made anywhere else silently vanished from that goal's numbers.

- transactions.ts: createManualTransaction now accepts a goalId (ignored
  unless the transaction is an INVESTMENT_CONTRIBUTION) and applies it via
  the same goal-progress logic the Sonhos screen uses, so progress can't
  drift depending on which screen logged the money. deleteTransaction now
  reverses that effect when a contribution transaction is deleted.
- goals.ts: extracted applyGoalContribution/reverseGoalContribution as the
  one shared place that logic lives, used by both addGoalContribution and
  the new transactions.ts path.
- aggregations.ts: goals of type EMERGENCY_FUND now always display the
  live-computed reserve (bank balances + liquid investments) instead of a
  manually-tracked column, so the reserva de emergência never disagrees
  with itself between the Sonhos screen and the Ponteiro/dashboard. The
  Sonhos screen's "Aportar" input is hidden for that goal type since its
  number isn't something you log by hand.

Retirement's own progress (currentNetWorth) already recomputes live on
every save, so it needed no change here.

